      "problem": "Factor $6{c}^{4}-19{c}^{2}-7.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $z={c}^{2}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $s:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{c}^{4}-19{c}^{2}-7 & =6{({c}^{2})}^{2}-19{c}^{2}-7 \\\\  & =6{z}^{2}-19z-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{z}^{2}-19z-7 & =(3z+1)(2z-7) \\\\  & =(3{c}^{2}+1)(2{c}^{2}-7)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
